# Test Case Review Summary

Whenever you write or substantially update problem tests, **always include a
markdown summary table in the chat reply** so the user can review coverage
without opening every test method. Do not wait to be asked.

## Required table columns

| Column | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Group | Nested class / category name |
| Test | Method name |
| Input (brief) | Compact description or key shape of input |
| Expected | What the assertion checks |
| Why it matters | Edge / example / property under test |

## Guidance

- One row per `@Test` (or parameterized case family).
- Keep cells short; prefer shapes like `3x3, zero at center` over full matrices.
- Group rows in the same order as the test file.
- If tests already existed and you only add a few, summarize the new ones and
  note that the rest are unchanged — or provide the full table if small.
- Still follow existing test style in the repo (`@Nested`, `@DisplayName`, etc.).
